12.steps:
step 1: go to Network page, open configuration Window for primary WAN, select IP Assignment as PPPoE, fill in user name and password as appropriate, accept default settings for all other options, and click OK;
step 2: verify from the GUI that primary WAN can receive correct IP address;
step 3: verify Network -> Address Objects page that WAN subnets, WAN Interface IP, All WAN IP, and All WAN Management IP are shown the correct information

14.steps:
step 1: go to Network page, open configuration Window for primary WAN, select IP Assignment as PPPoE, fill in user name and password as appropriate, accept default settings for all other options, and click OK;
step 2: go to Network page, open configuration Window for secondary WAN, select IP Assignment as PPPoE, fill in user name and password as appropriate, accept default settings for all other options, and click OK;
step 3: verify from the GUI that both primary and secondary WAN can receive correct IP address

19.steps:
step 1: go to Network page, open configuration Window for WAN, select IP Assignment as PPPoE, fill in user name and password as appropriate, check Inactivity Disconnect and accept default setting (10 minutes), and click OK;
step 2: verify from the GUI that primary WAN can receive correct IP address;
step 3: keep SonicWALL inactive for 10 minutes without any traffic from LAN->WAN;
step 4: verify that PPPoE connection is terminated;
